site/

# Python, for the measurement and figure tools under research/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# research/ - the measurement material and the record written from it.
#
# The WRITING is repository content and is tracked: research/README.md (the full record), every
# analysis document, every packet, and the measurement and capture tools that produced the numbers.
# About 2.5 MB of text, so the claims in docs/ can always be traced to the work behind them.
#
# The MATERIAL is not: iOS captures, the mac rig session, device captures, decoded arrays, figures
# and APKs come to about 6 GB, and the competitor clones are other projects' repositories. They live
# in the working tree on purpose (AGENTS.md and research/README.md explain why) but GitHub cannot
# carry them.
#
# The leading slash anchors these to the repository root, so docs/research/ - the published
# write-ups - is untouched by them.
/research/**
!/research/**/
!/research/**/*.md
!/research/**/*.py
!/research/**/*.sh
!/research/**/*.csv
!/research/**/*.txt
# The before/after figures the record's argument rests on: 1.6 MB, and a claim about what the page
# does at a bar's edge is worth little without the picture of it.
!/research/analysis/v3/figures/*.png
# ...except these, which are data or other people's code however they are spelled.
/research/datasets/
/research/competitors/
/research/**/__pycache__/

# Private iterative corpus; curated final evidence is published in review/.
/research/analysis/v3/astra-independent/

# Private consolidated build environment and recovery material
/.local/
/batch_run.log

# Web adapter development/test output
node_modules/
playwright-report/
test-results/
